  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4f7f3a59-8bdf-5ca9-a23c-fb74720c64b4" activityNameId="68a4c14f-caee-5cd0-bf7e-a284b2583a17" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Reclaimed asphalt pavement (RAP), at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Reclaimed asphalt pavement (RAP), at plant
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 3ef03caa-45be-4182-94d1-1e755bc4310c
The process and material data for the production of RAP were determined through a survey of 11 asphalt plants that produce these recycling material. According to estimates, the surveyed asphalt plants produce approx. 860'000 tons of reclaimed asphalt, which corresponds to about 40% of the annually produced asphalt granulate of 2.1 million tons. A distinction was made between RAP produced in diesel-powered plants and RAP produced in electrically powered plants. This distinction arises from the fact that, in some facilities, mobile processing plants are used that are powered by diesel. The life cycle inventories of these two types of plants differ only in the energy source used. The life cycle inventories of these two types of plants differ only in the energy source applied. For this life cycle inventory, a distribution of 50% diesel-powered and 50% electrically powered plants was assumed.The machines used for material handling (wheel loaders/hydraulic excavators) are represented by the process “Building machine/RER/1 U” as well as by scaled quantities of lubricating oil based on the process “diesel, burned in building machine, with particle filter/MJ/CH” and the disposal of waste oil.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Production of reclaimed asphalt, with 50% from diesel-powered and 50% from electrically powered plants.
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 860'000 t
Sampling: Survey 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3ef03caa-45be-4182-94d1-1e755bc4310c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
